<title>SPAIN: Spanish Treasury announces bond, note tenders.</title>
<headline>Spanish Treasury announces bond, note tenders.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain announced on Monday  BANDF the amount of notes and bonds the Treasury would tender at its monthly auctions on Tuesday and Wednesday.</p>
<p>Following are the minimum and maximum amounts:</p>
<p>(in billions of pesetas)</p>
<p> ISSUE	   Expected amount   Maximum amount     Auction date</p>
<p> 3 and 10-yr	225		    275		  Feb 4 5</p>
<p> 15-yr		175		    225		  Feb 5</p>
<p>    January auctions	amount announced   allotted</p>
<p>    10/1 (3- and 10-year)	275 - 325	250 *</p>
<p>    10/2 (5- and 15-year)	200 - 250	255 *</p>
<p>* This is the amount actually sold on the market and includes the second segment of the auction.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
